{
 "_doc": "Remington 870 gunfire: same layer set as the AK. 12 ga: huge low-mid blast, little crack. close = Herrington 11-87 report (wide stereo) + SRM-12 / Mk14 body weight; sub is deeper and longer; mech is the recoil thump of the receiver / forend (the pump itself is its own element, fired from the Pump clip). Round 4: fire_sub is built from real recordings only (low-passed shot + the same shot pitched down); no synthesis. Round 4: no algorithmic reverb anywhere; the far layer is the real recorded tail, low-passed and compressed. Round 5 (2026-10-03 revamp): 8 close variants over the three Herrington recordings, each layered with a different shot of the real Remington 870 (Audiobeast, medium warehouse, 10 m: 80 Hz - 2.5 kHz, 7 dB down) for the gun's own boom, SRM-12 / Mk14 weight or the TS Sound 12-gauge crack on some; chain eased for crest. Round 6 (2026-10-03): the close layer rebuilt from the Tactical Shooter Pack only, on the AK's recipe - the pack's SRM-12 shotgun shot (the Herrington takes start soft and clip flat 40-60 ms in) under a TR15 crack (high-passed), an R08 / WK-11 mid layer (150 Hz - 5 kHz) and Mk14 weight, variety from the layers and +-0.9 st, through the AK's chain with a shotgun's low end - so both guns share one recording style. (The Audiobeast warehouse and TS Sound layers are gone from it.)",
